FIVE EVERYDAY NETWORKED DEVICES AND THEIR NETWORK TYPES
=======================================================

1. SMARTPHONE
   Network type: WAN (mobile data) and LAN (home/office WiFi)
   Details: Uses 4G/5G cell towers to reach the wider internet, and
   switches to WiFi when it is available.

2. WIFI ROUTER
   Network type: LAN, bridging to a WAN
   Details: Creates the local network for your devices and connects it
   to your internet provider, which is the WAN.

3. SMART TV
   Network type: LAN
   Details: Joins the router over WiFi or Ethernet to stream content
   from the internet.

4. LAPTOP
   Network type: LAN (WiFi or Ethernet) and PAN (Bluetooth)
   Details: Gets internet through the router, and pairs with a mouse,
   keyboard, or earbuds over Bluetooth.

5. SMARTWATCH
   Network type: PAN
   Details: Pairs with your phone over Bluetooth, usually within a few
   meters.


QUICK REFRESHER ON NETWORK TYPES
--------------------------------
PAN (Personal Area Network): A very small range around one person,
    such as Bluetooth devices.
LAN (Local Area Network): A home, office, or building, such as WiFi
    or Ethernet.
WAN (Wide Area Network): A large geographic area. The internet is
    the biggest example.

Note: Many devices belong to more than one network at the same time.
Your phone, for example, can be on a PAN (with a smartwatch), a LAN
(home WiFi), and a WAN (mobile data) all at once.
